# The run directory is 4.8 GB and none of it belongs in git. Everything ignored
# here is regenerable from the code and configs that are tracked: the pipeline is
# seeded end to end and every run manifest carries the dataset hashes, so a
# rerun reproduces these bytes rather than approximating them.

# Model weights. Twelve branch checkpoints plus C0, at roughly 800 MB each.
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth

# Cached activations. Fourteen files of per-layer residuals over the Ω set,
# ~3.8 GB. These are an intermediate, not a result: the numbers computed from
# them are tracked as JSON.
**/hiddens/

# Tokenizer copies written into every checkpoint directory. Identical to the
# upstream Pythia tokenizer, 3.6 MB each, and meaningless without the weights
# they sit next to.
**/tokenizer.json
**/tokenizer_config.json
**/generation_config.json
**/special_tokens_map.json

# Environment and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local secrets. None are committed today and none should be: Modal and
# Hugging Face both authenticate from the ambient environment.
.env
.env.*
*.token

# The paper draft stays local. The article is the published account, and the
# draft still carries two citation errors (Krakovna 2020 is a blog post, and the
# Malmqvist 2025 description does not match arXiv:2505.07846) plus placeholder
# appendices. Publishing a known-wrong draft alongside a correct article invites
# people to quote the wrong one.
eae/paper/
